1
00:00:05,992 --> 00:00:14,505
Restoration and carbon projects are funded on claims: hectares
restored, vegetation recovered, trees surviving.

2
00:00:14,948 --> 00:00:21,536
Funders and auditors can rarely check those claims themselves,
or see where each number came from.

3
00:00:21,984 --> 00:00:29,940
GroundTruth is a screening tool for that gap. It lines up what
a project claims against what can be observed, and states

4
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:31,821
plainly what it cannot show.

5
00:00:32,261 --> 00:00:40,852
It is not a fraud detector, and it does not replace an audit.
A gap between claim and evidence is a reason to look closer,

6
00:00:40,892 --> 00:00:41,994
never a verdict.

7
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:51,068
The benchmark cases on this public page are simulated, and
labelled. Everything after this uses a project created live,

8
00:00:51,108 --> 00:00:52,904
with real satellite data.

9
00:00:55,771 --> 00:01:01,159
Let's follow a restoration NGO, signing in with a
demonstration account.

10
00:01:04,001 --> 00:01:12,304
What this user can open or change is decided by the server,
not the page. The dashboard also lists a shared reference

11
00:01:12,344 --> 00:01:15,828
project with no observations, so we open our own.

12
00:01:16,283 --> 00:01:25,183
This demonstration project is in the Sahyadri foothills near
Pune, India, created by uploading a hand-drawn boundary. It is

13
00:01:25,223 --> 00:01:27,015
not a registered project.

14
00:01:27,469 --> 00:01:36,492
The progress bar shows what is done: boundary, document,
satellite data, assessment and claims. Climate data is still

15
00:01:36,532 --> 00:01:37,117
missing.

16
00:01:42,791 --> 00:01:50,140
The boundary is stored with a checksum, and measured on an
equal-area projection: about two thousand and eighteen

17
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:50,734
hectares.

18
00:01:51,179 --> 00:01:59,387
On the Evidence tab the NGO uploads its design document,
stored with a SHA-256 checksum so it cannot be changed

19
00:01:59,427 --> 00:02:00,137
unnoticed.

20
00:02:00,579 --> 00:02:09,377
GroundTruth then lists the statements it recognises. This is
plain pattern matching, not a language model, and these are

21
00:02:09,417 --> 00:02:12,496
candidates only. Nothing here is verified.

22
00:02:12,945 --> 00:02:22,127
It found five: a restored area, a greenness change, sapling
survival, a carbon figure, and a rise in bird species

23
00:02:22,167 --> 00:02:22,868
richness.

24
00:02:23,321 --> 00:02:31,354
I have added all five as claims. Adding a claim does not
verify it, and the original wording stays beside it.

25
00:02:34,417 --> 00:02:42,919
To get satellite evidence, the NGO requests observations for
the boundary. A background worker downloads Sentinel-2 images

26
00:02:42,959 --> 00:02:48,709
from Microsoft Planetary Computer, masks cloud, and reduces
each year to one value.

27
00:02:49,162 --> 00:02:59,485
This request covered 2021 to 2026, January to March, at most
twenty percent cloud. It finished, with project-area coverage

28
00:02:59,525 --> 00:03:02,654
above ninety-five percent every year.

29
00:03:03,098 --> 00:03:11,742
The satellite's reflectance measurements are observations. The
indices computed from them, such as NDVI, are derived

30
00:03:11,782 --> 00:03:19,595
indicators, and each row is badged that way. A model estimate
would carry a diamond. There are none here.

31
00:03:20,051 --> 00:03:26,854
The table lists the exact scene identifiers behind each year,
so anyone can repeat the calculation.

32
00:03:27,297 --> 00:03:36,056
NDVI shows how green the land looks from space. It is not
carbon, tree survival or biodiversity, and these values are

33
00:03:36,096 --> 00:03:38,559
not validated against field data.

34
00:03:39,013 --> 00:03:48,886
The series is not a clean rise: greenness peaks in 2023, then
falls back. The assessment reads this as no clear change.

35
00:03:51,929 --> 00:03:56,683
On the verification tab, each claim is judged on its own
evidence.

36
00:03:57,130 --> 00:04:05,378
The area claim is only partly consistent. The claimed nineteen
hundred hectares fits inside the boundary, but a boundary

37
00:04:05,418 --> 00:04:09,557
shows where a project works, not how much land was restored.

38
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:21,052
The greenness claim, up 0.05, is consistent with the observed
change of about 0.051. That describes greenness. It does not

39
00:04:21,092 --> 00:04:23,527
show the project caused it.

40
00:04:23,982 --> 00:04:32,482
Three claims are marked not enough evidence to test: survival
needs field surveys, carbon needs biomass measurement or a

41
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:40,878
registry record, and bird species need wildlife surveys.
Unverified does not mean false. It means the evidence has not

42
00:04:40,918 --> 00:04:41,883
been supplied.

43
00:04:42,324 --> 00:04:51,092
Attribution is inconclusive: there are no observations from
before treatment, no comparison areas and no climate series.

44
00:04:51,132 --> 00:04:53,831
So GroundTruth makes no causal claim.

45
00:04:56,870 --> 00:05:02,073
Everything the platform knows can be exported as a technical
dossier for an auditor.

46
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:11,297
The ZIP holds the assessment, claims, observations with scene
identifiers, documents and provenance, with a checksum

47
00:05:11,337 --> 00:05:11,988
manifest.

48
00:05:12,439 --> 00:05:19,826
Each download is sealed in an audit ledger. Records are
chained to one another, and the page recomputes the chain

49
00:05:19,866 --> 00:05:21,152
every time it loads.

50
00:05:21,601 --> 00:05:29,767
The new report-sealed record appears here. The ledger is not
externally timestamped or signed, so it detects alteration,

51
00:05:29,807 --> 00:05:34,388
deletion and reordering, but cannot prove when a record was
written.

52
00:05:34,832 --> 00:05:42,568
In testing, altering one stored record in the database made
the page report a failed integrity check. Restoring it

53
00:05:42,608 --> 00:05:44,769
returned the status to verified.

54
00:05:49,758 --> 00:05:58,450
The funder has view access. They can read claims, observations
and the ledger, but see no upload or request controls, and the

55
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:02,535
server refuses those actions even when attempted directly.

56
00:06:07,542 --> 00:06:14,230
The auditor can download the dossier, and check any file they
were given against the ledger record that sealed it.

57
00:06:14,684 --> 00:06:19,782
Here, the file is confirmed byte-for-byte identical to the
sealed report.

58
00:06:21,938 --> 00:06:30,436
This is an early screening tool. Next: observations from
before a project began, climate and comparison-area data so

59
00:06:30,476 --> 00:06:35,930
attribution becomes possible, and field validation of the
satellite values.

60
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:42,998
GroundTruth. What was claimed, what was observed, and what
cannot yet be shown.
